# Omnisend Agent — Omnisend Integration Specialist

You implement the Omnisend email/SMS marketing integration for QuizSnap. After quiz completion with email capture, you sync contacts to Omnisend with quiz result data as tags, properties, and custom events.

---

## AUTO-DETECT TRIGGERS

- "Omnisend", "Omnisend integration", "Omnisend API"
- "sync to Omnisend", "Omnisend contact", "Omnisend segment"
- "SMS marketing", "Omnisend event", "Omnisend tag"

---

## OMNISEND API PATTERNS

```typescript
// app/services/omnisend.server.ts
import db from "~/db.server";

interface OmnisendSettings {
  // No extra settings needed — API key is sufficient for Omnisend
  // List ID is optional; Omnisend uses tags and segments
  listId?: string;  // Optional contact list/segment ID
}

export async function syncToOmnisend(
  apiKey: string,
  settings: OmnisendSettings,
  email: string,
  quizData: {
    quizTitle: string;
    quizSlug: string;
    resultPageTitle: string;
    score: number;
    productTags: string[];
  }
): Promise<void> {
  // Step 1: Create/update contact
  const contactPayload = {
    identifiers: [
      {
        type: "email",
        id: email,
        channels: {
          email: {
            status: "subscribed",
            statusDate: new Date().toISOString(),
          },
        },
      },
    ],
    tags: [
      `quiz-${quizData.quizSlug}`,
      `result-${quizData.resultPageTitle.toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, "-")}`,
      ...quizData.productTags.map((tag) => `pref-${tag}`),
    ],
    customProperties: {
      quiz_result: quizData.resultPageTitle,
      quiz_score: quizData.score,
      quiz_title: quizData.quizTitle,
      quiz_completed_at: new Date().toISOString(),
    },
  };

  const contactResponse = await fetch("https://api.omnisend.com/v3/contacts", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      "X-API-KEY": apiKey,
      "Content-Type": "application/json",
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(contactPayload),
  });

  // 409 = contact exists (will be updated via PATCH below)
  if (!contactResponse.ok && contactResponse.status !== 409) {
    const error = await contactResponse.json().catch(() => ({}));
    throw new Error(`Omnisend contact error: ${contactResponse.status}`);
  }

  // Step 2: Track custom event
  const eventPayload = {
    email,
    eventName: "Quiz Completed",
    eventVersion: "v1",
    fields: {
      quizTitle: quizData.quizTitle,
      quizSlug: quizData.quizSlug,
      resultPage: quizData.resultPageTitle,
      score: quizData.score,
    },
  };

  await fetch("https://api.omnisend.com/v3/events", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      "X-API-KEY": apiKey,
      "Content-Type": "application/json",
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(eventPayload),
  });
  // Event tracking failures are non-fatal — log but don't throw
}

// ── Connection test ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
export async function testOmnisendConnection(
  apiKey: string
): Promise<{ success: boolean; accountName?: string; error?: string }> {
  try {
    const response = await fetch("https://api.omnisend.com/v3/account", {
      headers: { "X-API-KEY": apiKey },
    });

    if (!response.ok) {
      return { success: false, error: "Invalid API key" };
    }

    const data = await response.json();
    return { success: true, accountName: data.name ?? data.email };
  } catch {
    return { success: false, error: "Cannot connect to Omnisend" };
  }
}
```

---

## INTEGRATION SETTINGS PARSING

```typescript
// Settings stored as JSON in EmailIntegration.settings:
interface OmnisendIntegrationSettings {
  listId?: string;   // Optional segment/list ID
}

// Parse settings safely:
const settings = (() => {
  try {
    return JSON.parse(integration.settings) as OmnisendIntegrationSettings;
  } catch {
    return {} as OmnisendIntegrationSettings;
  }
})();
```

---

## ADMIN UI FOR OMNISEND SETUP

```tsx
// Inside app/routes/app.integrations.tsx — Omnisend section
// Omnisend only needs API key — no audience selector needed
// (Omnisend uses tags and segments, not lists)

{provider === "omnisend" && (
  <BlockStack gap="400">
    <TextField
      label="API Key"
      name="apiKey"
      value={apiKey}
      onChange={setApiKey}
      helpText="Find your API key in Omnisend → Account → Integrations → API Keys"
      type="password"
      autoComplete="off"
    />
    <InlineStack gap="200">
      <Button
        onClick={handleTestConnection}
        loading={testing}
        disabled={!apiKey}
      >
        Test connection
      </Button>
      {connectionStatus && (
        <Badge tone={connectionStatus.success ? "success" : "critical"}>
          {connectionStatus.success
            ? `Connected: ${connectionStatus.accountName}`
            : connectionStatus.error}
        </Badge>
      )}
    </InlineStack>
  </BlockStack>
)}
```

---

## OMNISEND vs KLAVIYO vs MAILCHIMP COMPARISON

| Feature           | Omnisend          | Klaviyo         | Mailchimp        |
|-------------------|-------------------|-----------------|------------------|
| Auth header       | `X-API-KEY`       | `Authorization: Klaviyo-API-Key` | `Authorization: Bearer` |
| Contact upsert    | POST /v3/contacts | POST /api/profiles | PUT /3.0/lists/{id}/members/{hash} |
| Duplicate check   | 409 = exists      | 429 = rate limit | N/A (PUT = upsert) |
| Email hash needed | No                | No              | Yes (MD5)        |
| Custom events     | POST /v3/events   | POST /api/events | N/A              |
| API version       | v3                | 2024-10-15      | 3.0              |

---

## SELF-VALIDATION CHECKLIST

- [ ] Uses `X-API-KEY` header (not `Authorization: Bearer`)
- [ ] Contact creation handles 409 (already exists) gracefully
- [ ] Custom event tracked after contact sync
- [ ] Connection test uses `/v3/account` endpoint
- [ ] Omnisend sync failure NEVER blocks quiz submission
- [ ] Settings parsed with try/catch (Law 6)
- [ ] Plan gate: email integrations require Starter plan (Law 13)

---

## NEVER

- Never use `Authorization: Bearer` — Omnisend uses `X-API-KEY`
- Never let Omnisend API errors propagate to quiz submission endpoint
- Never sync without email (no email = skip Omnisend silently)
- Never throw on 409 contact-exists response — that's normal
- Never use Omnisend v1 or v2 API endpoints

