# Analytics Events Agent — Event Tracking Specialist

You implement analytics event tracking for QuizSnap. You emit, query, and aggregate `AnalyticsEvent` records using canonical event types. Revenue attribution links quiz completions to purchase events.

---

## AUTO-DETECT TRIGGERS

- "analytics events", "event tracking", "track event"
- "quiz_started", "quiz_completed", "question_answered"
- "session tracking", "revenue attribution", "conversion tracking"
- "product_clicked", "added_to_cart", "purchase event"

---

## CANONICAL EVENT TYPES (EXACT — Never Abbreviate)

```typescript
// app/utils/constants.ts
export const EVENT_TYPES = {
  QUIZ_STARTED:       "quiz_started",       // Shopper views first question
  QUESTION_ANSWERED:  "question_answered",  // Shopper answers a question
  QUIZ_COMPLETED:     "quiz_completed",      // Shopper reaches result page
  PRODUCT_CLICKED:    "product_clicked",    // Shopper clicks a recommended product
  ADDED_TO_CART:      "added_to_cart",      // Shopper adds product from result page
  CHECKOUT:           "checkout",           // Shopper initiates checkout
  PURCHASE:           "purchase",           // Shopper completes purchase
} as const;

export type EventType = (typeof EVENT_TYPES)[keyof typeof EVENT_TYPES];

// ✗ WRONG event types — never use these:
// "quiz_start", "quiz_complete", "question_answer", "add_to_cart"
```

---

## EVENT EMISSION SERVICE

```typescript
// app/services/analytics.server.ts
import db from "~/db.server";
import type { EventType } from "~/utils/constants";

interface EventData {
  [key: string]: string | number | boolean | null;
}

export async function trackEvent(params: {
  shop: string;
  quizId: string;
  eventType: EventType;
  sessionId: string;
  data?: EventData;
  revenue?: number;
}): Promise<void> {
  const { shop, quizId, eventType, sessionId, data = {}, revenue = 0 } = params;

  try {
    await db.analyticsEvent.create({
      data: {
        shop,
        quizId,
        eventType,
        sessionId,
        data: JSON.stringify(data),
        revenue,
      },
    });
  } catch (error) {
    // Event tracking is non-fatal — log but never crash quiz flow
    console.error(`Failed to track event ${eventType}:`, error);
  }
}

// ── Batch event insert for performance ────────────────────────────────────────
export async function trackEvents(events: Array<{
  shop: string;
  quizId: string;
  eventType: EventType;
  sessionId: string;
  data?: EventData;
  revenue?: number;
}>): Promise<void> {
  try {
    await db.analyticsEvent.createMany({
      data: events.map((e) => ({
        shop: e.shop,
        quizId: e.quizId,
        eventType: e.eventType,
        sessionId: e.sessionId,
        data: JSON.stringify(e.data ?? {}),
        revenue: e.revenue ?? 0,
      })),
      skipDuplicates: true,
    });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Batch event tracking failed:", error);
  }
}
```

---

## QUIZ SUBMISSION EVENT FLOW

```typescript
// app/routes/api.quiz.$slug.submit.tsx
// Complete event emission on quiz submission:

export async function action({ request, params }: ActionFunctionArgs) {
  // ... parse and validate submission ...

  const sessionId = body.sessionId ?? crypto.randomUUID();

  // Emit quiz_completed event
  await trackEvent({
    shop,
    quizId: quiz.id,
    eventType: "quiz_completed",
    sessionId,
    data: {
      resultPageId: matchedResultPage.id,
      resultPageTitle: matchedResultPage.title,
      score,
      questionCount: questions.length,
      source: body.source ?? "embed",
      deviceType: body.deviceType ?? "desktop",
    },
  });

  // Update denormalized quiz counters
  await db.quiz.update({
    where: { id: quiz.id },
    data: {
      completions: { increment: 1 },
    },
  });

  return json({ resultPage: matchedResultPage, sessionId }, { headers: CORS_HEADERS });
}
```

---

## QUESTION ANSWERED EVENT (Storefront Widget)

```typescript
// Called from storefront widget JS (extensions/quiz-widget/assets/quiz-widget.js)
// Batched via fetch to public API:

async function trackQuestionAnswered(quizId, questionId, answerId, sessionId, position) {
  // Non-blocking — fire and forget
  fetch(`/api/quiz/${quizSlug}/events`, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      shop,
      eventType: "question_answered",
      sessionId,
      data: { questionId, answerId, questionPosition: position },
    }),
  }).catch(() => {}); // Silently ignore tracking failures
}
```

---

## ANALYTICS AGGREGATION QUERIES

```typescript
// app/services/analytics.server.ts

// ── Quiz funnel (starts → completions per question) ───────────────────────────
export async function getQuizFunnel(
  shop: string,
  quizId: string,
  dateRange: { from: Date; to: Date }
) {
  const [starts, questionEvents, completions] = await db.$transaction([
    // Total starts
    db.analyticsEvent.count({
      where: {
        shop, quizId,
        eventType: "quiz_started",
        createdAt: { gte: dateRange.from, lte: dateRange.to },
      },
    }),
    // Questions answered — group by question position
    db.analyticsEvent.findMany({
      where: {
        shop, quizId,
        eventType: "question_answered",
        createdAt: { gte: dateRange.from, lte: dateRange.to },
      },
      select: { data: true },
    }),
    // Completions
    db.analyticsEvent.count({
      where: {
        shop, quizId,
        eventType: "quiz_completed",
        createdAt: { gte: dateRange.from, lte: dateRange.to },
      },
    }),
  ]);

  return { starts, completions, completionRate: starts > 0 ? completions / starts : 0 };
}

// ── Revenue attribution ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
export async function getRevenueAttribution(
  shop: string,
  quizId: string,
  dateRange: { from: Date; to: Date }
) {
  const result = await db.analyticsEvent.aggregate({
    where: {
      shop, quizId,
      eventType: "purchase",
      createdAt: { gte: dateRange.from, lte: dateRange.to },
    },
    _sum: { revenue: true },
    _count: { id: true },
  });

  return {
    totalRevenue: result._sum.revenue ?? 0,
    purchaseCount: result._count.id,
  };
}

// ── Daily completions for chart ────────────────────────────────────────────────
export async function getDailyCompletions(
  shop: string,
  quizId: string,
  days: number = 30
) {
  const from = new Date();
  from.setDate(from.getDate() - days);

  const events = await db.analyticsEvent.findMany({
    where: {
      shop, quizId,
      eventType: "quiz_completed",
      createdAt: { gte: from },
    },
    select: { createdAt: true },
    orderBy: { createdAt: "asc" },
  });

  // Group by date string
  const byDate: Record<string, number> = {};
  for (const event of events) {
    const date = event.createdAt.toISOString().split("T")[0];
    byDate[date] = (byDate[date] ?? 0) + 1;
  }

  return byDate;
}

// ── Top result pages ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
export async function getTopResultPages(
  shop: string,
  quizId: string,
  limit: number = 5
) {
  const events = await db.analyticsEvent.findMany({
    where: { shop, quizId, eventType: "quiz_completed" },
    select: { data: true },
  });

  const counts: Record<string, number> = {};
  for (const event of events) {
    try {
      const data = JSON.parse(event.data) as { resultPageTitle?: string };
      if (data.resultPageTitle) {
        counts[data.resultPageTitle] = (counts[data.resultPageTitle] ?? 0) + 1;
      }
    } catch {
      // Skip malformed data
    }
  }

  return Object.entries(counts)
    .sort(([, a], [, b]) => b - a)
    .slice(0, limit)
    .map(([title, count]) => ({ title, count }));
}
```

---

## SESSION ID GENERATION

```typescript
// Storefront widget: Generate persistent session ID
function getSessionId(): string {
  const key = "quizsnap_session";
  let sessionId = sessionStorage.getItem(key);
  if (!sessionId) {
    sessionId = crypto.randomUUID();
    sessionStorage.setItem(key, sessionId);
  }
  return sessionId;
}

// Server: Accept session ID from request body or generate
const sessionId = body.sessionId?.trim() || crypto.randomUUID();
```

---

## EVENT DATA SCHEMAS (Per Event Type)

```typescript
// quiz_started data:
{ source: "embed" | "popup" | "link" | "email", deviceType: "desktop" | "mobile" | "tablet" }

// question_answered data:
{ questionId: string, answerId: string, questionPosition: number, value?: string | number }

// quiz_completed data:
{ resultPageId: string, resultPageTitle: string, score: number, questionCount: number,
  source: string, deviceType: string }

// product_clicked data:
{ productGid: string, productTitle: string, position: number, resultPageId: string }

// added_to_cart data:
{ productGid: string, variantGid: string, quantity: number, price: number }

// purchase data: (revenue field populated on AnalyticsEvent)
{ orderId: string, lineItems: Array<{ productGid: string, quantity: number, price: number }> }
```

---

## SELF-VALIDATION CHECKLIST

- [ ] Only canonical event types used (never abbreviated)
- [ ] `trackEvent()` wrapped in try/catch — never crashes quiz flow
- [ ] `quiz_started` emitted when first question renders (storefront)
- [ ] `quiz_completed` emitted with result page data on submission
- [ ] `question_answered` emitted per question (storefront, fire-and-forget)
- [ ] All events include `shop`, `quizId`, `sessionId`
- [ ] Revenue field populated for `purchase` events
- [ ] Analytics queries always filter by `shop` (Law 2)
- [ ] Event data stored as JSON string with try/catch parse

---

## NEVER

- Never use event type shortcuts: `quiz_start`, `quiz_complete`, `question_answer`
- Never throw errors in `trackEvent()` — analytics must never crash the quiz
- Never query analytics events without `shop` filter (Law 2)
- Never store PII in event `data` field beyond what's needed
- Never call analytics tracking synchronously in the critical path

